{"name":"Back Stage","hex":"#6b625b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"back","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At or near the rear.","Returned or restored to a previous place or condition."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To or in a previous condition or place.","In a direction opposite to that in which someone or something is facing or normally pointing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back"},{"term":"stage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A phase.","One of the portions of a device (such as a rocket or thermonuclear weapon) which are used or activated in a particular order, one after another."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce on a stage, to perform a play.","To arrange in a manner intended to deceive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Back Stage (1923 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Back Stage is a 1923 silent Our Gang silent short subject comedy film directed by Robert F. McGowan, that is the 13th entry to be released."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Our_Gang_Back_Stage_1923.jpg/330px-Our_Gang_Back_Stage_1923.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Back_Stage_(1923_film)"},{"title":"Back Stage (1919 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Back Stage is a 1919 American two-reel silent comedy film directed by and starring Roscoe \"Fatty\" Arbuckle and featuring Buster Keaton and Al St. John."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Back_stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Back_Stage_(1919_film)"},{"title":"Backstage (publication)","blocks":[{"text":"Backstage, also previously written as Back Stage, is a global casting platform and entertainment industry publication that connects performers, content creators, and behind-the-scenes professionals with casting directors and production teams across film, television, theater, commercials, and digital media."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0d/Backstage_Cover_June_9%2C_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backstage_(publication)"},{"title":"Human back","blocks":[{"text":"The human back, also called the dorsum, is the large posterior area of the human body, rising from the top of the buttocks to the back of the neck. It is the surface of the body opposite from the chest and the abdomen. The vertebral column runs the length of the back and creates a central area of recession. The breadth of the back is created by the shoulders at the top and the pelvis at the bottom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_back"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Back_Stage_%281919%29_-_3.jpg/330px-Back_Stage_%281919%29_-_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Back_Stage_%281919%29_-_3.jpg/330px-Back_Stage_%281919%29_-_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Molly Malone and Roscoe \"Fatty\" Arbuckle in Back Stage.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABack_Stage_(1919)_-_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/120px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/250px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna